Lab 1 — xv6 and Unix Utilities

Focus: xv6 fundamentals, C, system calls, processes, file descriptors, pointers, and Unix-style utilities.

Completed
Boot xv6 — Built and ran xv6 on RISC-V using QEMU; explored the xv6 shell, processes, and filesystem.
sleep — Implemented a user-level sleep program using command-line arguments, atoi(), and the pause() system call.
sixfive — Implemented a text-processing utility using open(), read(), C strings, and character parsing.
memdump — Implemented memory inspection using C pointers and interpreted raw memory according to a format string.
find — Implemented recursive directory traversal using open(), read(), fstat(), and C string operations.
find -exec — Extended find to execute a command for each matching file using fork(), exec(), and wait().
